  "vendor_website": "dlg.com.br",
  "description": "16-channel universal remote I/O (thermocouple, Pt100, current, voltage, frequency, logic) with two relay alarms and two independent RS485 Modbus RTU ports",
  "revision": 1,
  "revised": "2026-11-18",
  "firmware": "Manual 01.00_16 (response delay from V1.1.0)",
  "source": "DLG Automação Industrial, XM-210 user manual MAN-PT-DE-XM210-01.00_16 (Portuguese)",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Universal Remote Modbus XM-210 - Manual do usuário",
      "version": "MAN-PT-DE-XM210-01.00_16",
      "url": "https://www.dlg.com.br/manuaisdownload/MAN-PT-DE-XM210.pdf",
      "note": "Modbus table and register types",
      "accessed": "2026-11-18",
      "sha256": "b1122d72484589a1ea01c9ff85c25853769764ce883caac448f3a9ed406d4a29"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU over RS485, two independent ports (channel 1 on terminals 36 +, 35 -; channel 2 on 69 +, 68 -). The LT version has one port and only thermocouple inputs. Speeds 1200 to 115200 bit/s, even, odd or no parity.",
    "The manual lists the registers as 40001 on; the map uses 40001 less one, as sent on the wire. The mnemonic column of the manual's table is shifted by one row against the descriptions; this map follows the descriptions and the register numbers named in the manual's own text (status 40020, relay command 40022, speeds 40024 and 40027, delays 40026 and 40029, sensor types 40030 to 40045).",
    "Values are signed 16-bit integers with the decimal places set in each channel's decimal point register. The scale is -30000 to +30000 engineering units.",
    "Holding the reset button while the device is on sets address 1, 19200 bit/s and no parity temporarily on both ports; powering up with the button held restores the factory data.",
    "The sensor type table of the manual has two columns that disagree for the values 8 to 11. The values here follow the numbered column, which also matches the XM-102, XM-112 and I-210 manuals: Pt100 is 8, 0-20 mA 9, 4-20 mA 10, and 11 is the 0-75 input printed as V in this manual (0-100 mV on the sister models).",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "unit_id": 1,
  "databits": 8,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
  "enums": {
    "input_type": {"0": "Thermocouple J", "1": "Thermocouple K", "2": "Thermocouple T", "3": "Thermocouple R", "4": "Thermocouple S", "5": "Thermocouple E", "6": "Thermocouple N", "7": "Thermocouple B", "8": "Pt100", "9": "0-20 mA", "10": "4-20 mA", "11": "0-100 mV", "12": "0-5 V", "13": "0-10 V", "14": "Logic level", "15": "No input", "16": "Frequency"},
    "baud": {"0": "1200 bit/s", "1": "2400 bit/s", "2": "4800 bit/s", "3": "9600 bit/s", "4": "19200 bit/s", "5": "38400 bit/s", "6": "57600 bit/s", "7": "115200 bit/s"},
    "parity": {"0": "Even", "1": "Odd", "2": "None"},
    "alarm_cond": {"0": "Minimum value", "1": "Maximum value", "2": "Differential", "3": "Inoperative"}
  },
